{"signature": "{\"text\": \"Here is a GCSE-style question about interpreting a graph of renewable energy generation over several decades. Part A, worth two marks: explain why electricity generated from wood-based biomass might increase more slowly than electricity from some other renewables. A suitable answer, if supported by the graph and context, is that sustainably available biomass feedstock is limited and expanding production can compete with land needed for food or conservation. Award one mark for a relevant constraint and one for explaining how it limits growth. Part B, worth two marks: explain why wind power output can vary even when the number of turbines increases. A model answer is: wind speed varies with weather conditions, so turbines do not operate at rated power continuously; therefore, the amount of electricity generated changes even with the same installed capacity. Award one mark for variable wind conditions and one for linking this to changing output.\", \"voice\": \"en-NG-AbeoNeural\", \"rate\": \"-4%\", \"eleven\": false}", "duration": 58.632, "words": [["Here", 0.102083], ["is", 0.323458], ["a", 0.440625], ["GCSE-style", 0.557833], ["question", 1.391166], ["about", 1.781791], ["interpreting", 2.146375], ["a", 2.771375], ["graph", 2.914583], ["of", 3.188041], ["renewable", 3.370333], ["energy", 3.865125], ["generation", 4.294791], ["over", 4.906791], ["several", 5.167208], ["decades.", 5.570833], ["Part", 7.070333], ["A,", 7.356791], ["worth", 7.825541], ["two", 8.151041], ["marks:", 8.307291], ["explain", 8.919291], ["why", 9.401041], ["electricity", 9.505208], ["generated", 10.169291], ["from", 10.690125], ["wood-based", 10.9375], ["biomass", 11.39325], ["might", 11.888041], ["increase", 12.135416], ["more", 12.539083], ["slowly", 12.747416], ["than", 13.138041], ["electricity", 13.28125], ["from", 13.945333], ["some", 14.179708], ["other", 14.388041], ["renewables.", 14.648458], ["A", 16.237], ["suitable", 16.39325], ["answer,", 16.862], ["if